    "done_when": "The defect, measured by the coordinator at main 2ff0c2962: reckon.crew.obligations.obligations('reckon', 's21-1c') takes 64 s cold and 37.7 s warm. With _record_filed_elsewhere stubbed out it takes 19.4 s, so the S21 session's UserPromptSubmit hook (reckon/hooks/coordinator_obligations.py, 30 s limit) times out intermittently. The profile shows 44 calls of _record_filed_elsewhere performing about 1.46 million json.loads over a review store of about 1,586 entries. That is a whole-store rescan for every completed pointer, including runs whose review exists at their .at-sha path.\n\nFirst establish why the fallback is reached for a run whose review sits at its expected .at-sha path, and record the answer in the manifest.\n\nThen make the fallback:\n- not run when a record exists at the run's expected bare or .at-sha path;\n- otherwise answer from an index of reviewed_run_id to record path, built at most once per process and per store directory, and rebuilt when the directory's stat identity changes.\nThe misfiled case still returns the record flagged as misfiled.\n\nIn a new tests/test_misfiled_lookup_is_indexed.py, built on a synthesised store of at least 3,000 records under the test's temporary path:\n- many misses read each record file at most once, counted by patching the file read;\n- a run whose record is at its .at-sha path never reaches the scan;\n- a misfiled record is still found and flagged;\n- adding a record to the store is seen on the next call.\nThe named negative control (the index disabled so every miss rescans) is executed and fails the read-once case.\n\nMeasurement, not a test, as a log under the run directory: time obligations('reckon', 's21-1c') at base and at head on the real store, cold, in a fresh process each. Head must be no more than 3 s above the stubbed figure of 19.4 s.\n\nThe gate is the new test plus tests/test_review_store_finds_a_misfiled_record.py, tests/test_review_counts_added_failures.py, tests/test_logged_revision_forms.py and tests/test_a_promoted_row_names_its_reviewed_revision.py, run at base and at head. Evidence rules:\n- each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder;\n- each log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code;\n- every pytest process uses a basetemp private to that process;\n- the head arm adds no failure id;\n- ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed Python paths report no finding the base did not.\n\nScratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete. An evidence fragment at docs/evidence/fragments/scoring-should-stop-a-promotion/misfiled-lookup-is-indexed.html records the cause and both timings. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Make the misfiled-review fallback in reckon/crew/review.py cheap enough that the coordinator obligations hook stays well inside its 30 s limit, landing followup f-ssp-misfiled-lookup-is-indexed of scoring-should-stop-a-promotion.",
